"""patch_docs_g6_close_1029.py (2026-10-29): closes gate G6 in docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md and updates docs/THEORY.md section 9.
Records the by-era and by-number-of-terms report, the three-term rule, the frozen status of `diverged`, the enlarged G7 scope (36 positives and the
Tier 1 nulls, all tested before the 10-26 fix) and the ledger evidence gap. Both files are gated on their exact installed hashes; every replacement
must match exactly once; nothing is written unless all do. Usage: python3 scripts/audit/patch_docs_g6_close_1029.py [docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md] [docs/THEORY.md]"""
import hashlib, sys
def sha(s): return hashlib.sha256((s if s.endswith("\n") else s + "\n").encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()
sp = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md"
tp = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else "docs/THEORY.md"
S = open(sp, encoding="utf-8").read(); T = open(tp, encoding="utf-8").read()
assert sha(S) == "69473cf40f62a6ad7848b023b01cf8f681e1f8937608d4a0fb77844b40c2c40a", "PROJECT_STATUS is not the expected version; nothing changed"
assert sha(T) == "eddac4927de8a8d68ec6ecda800fa3dc1d16eae40e6deb583a78b0c9bff976da", "THEORY is not the expected version; nothing changed"
def sub(text, old, new, label):
    n = text.count(old); assert n == 1, "%s: expected exactly 1 match, found %d; nothing was written" % (label, n)
    print("ok  ", label); return text.replace(old, new)

S = sub(S, "STILL OPEN in G6: report by era and number of terms, then the fate of `diverged`. The values in the early rows still come from later filings and may reflect restatements | open |",
 "**REPORTED 10-29, by era and number of terms:** 14,176 of the 23,348 rows have a state (60.7 percent); coverage by event year is 4 percent in 2008 (38 of 1,053), 28 percent in 2009, 69 percent in 2010, 87 percent in 2011 and 91 to 99 percent from 2012 on; 1,820 rows have a period but no composite score (1,266 of them in 2008 to 2010). The states are THIN in every era: 13 percent rest on all four terms (1,895), 39 percent on three (5,519) and 48 percent on one or two (2,179 and 4,583); the extreme labels (deteriorating plus strong) fall as terms rise: 63.4 percent of one-term states, 47.7 percent of two-term, 43.1 percent of three-term, 39.1 percent of four-term. RULE: any test conditioned on the state uses states with 3 or more terms (7,414, 52 percent) as the primary analysis and reports the one- and two-term states separately. NOT YET CHECKED: which sectors produce the thin states (a three-term filter may drop banks and utilities). `diverged` stays FROZEN as decided on 2026-10-28: the 2,380 legacy tags remain, none is added, and none is a finding about the firm state. The values in the early rows still come from later filings and may reflect restatements, and the cut-points of the five labels are whole-history quantiles | **DONE 10-29, with limits** |", "S G6 close")
S = sub(S, "(rerun on the corrected data: 314 ripple events were added 10-28 and 508 events left the analysis set 10-29; re-measure independence, which was 69.8% on 10-28; 3 of the 15 only say a type uses the pooled number) | open |",
 "(rerun on the corrected data: 314 ripple events were added 10-28 and 508 events left the analysis set 10-29; re-measure independence, which was 69.8% on 10-28; 3 of the 15 only say a type uses the pooled number). **SCOPE ENLARGED 10-29:** every proven flag (15), every lead (21) and 60 of the 62 nulls were tested before the 10-26 tagger fix (the other 2 on 10-26 to 10-27), so none has been measured on the cleaned data. Also in G7: the 21 leads and the Tier 1 nulls (event_lasting_days_6_20, event_pre_days_m4_m1, time_to_threshold_asymmetry, direction_overreaction_reversal, tag_specific_ranges, event_type_financial_result, event_type_regulatory), each under its REGISTERED rule with the prediction (old estimate, old n, direction, range) written first. Tier 2, only if Tier 1 moves anything: magnitude_model_features, storm_x_sentiment, event_date_lag, event_label_signed_pull_center, event_band_class_calibration_audit, earnings_surprise_sign_revenue, earnings_surprise_size_revenue, event_gov_direct_burst, event_gov_direct_enforcement_burst, event_gov_direct_size_split (and, uncertain, size_effect_in_universe and volatility_estimator_variants). Not affected (tested on market-wide stock-days): the other 43 nulls. MULTIPLICITY RULE: a null that flips counts only if it passes its registered rule, clears a pre-stated minimum effect, and holds once on the sealed tickers (19 re-tests expect about one false pass); every result, including no change, is an append-only ledger note. The frozen forward tests are NOT re-run | open |", "S G7 scope")
S = sub(S, "(d) the independence figure (69.8%) predates 508 exclusions and must be re-measured (G7).",
 "(d) the independence figure (69.8%) predates 508 exclusions and must be re-measured (G7); (e) 9 of the 19 event-level candidate nulls (direction_overreaction_reversal, time_to_threshold_asymmetry, storm_x_sentiment, size_effect_in_universe, magnitude_model_features, tag_specific_ranges, volatility_estimator_variants, event_label_signed_pull_center, event_date_lag) and 6 leads have no stored evidence rows in flag_ledger_evidence (their numbers are only in their notes), and storm_tier_large's unit is inferred, its result file lost; the evidence is to be backfilled as append-only rows before the re-run.", "S evidence gap")
T = sub(T, "- **A point-in-time firm state** (gate G6): until then no label that depends on firm state, including `diverged`, can be tested.",
 "- **State-dependent hypotheses** (gate G6 is done, with limits, on 2026-10-29): the point-in-time state now exists (event_firm_state_pit2: 14,176 states, the first on 2008-09-25, 48 percent of them resting on only one or two terms), so labels that depend on firm state can be tested for the first time, each as a NEW pre-registered hypothesis (prediction, rule and forward window written first) with states of three or more terms (7,414) as the primary analysis; `diverged` stays frozen.", "T section 9")
open(sp, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(S); open(tp, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(T)
print("STATUS sha256", sha(S), "|", S.count("\n"), "lines"); print("THEORY sha256", sha(T), "|", T.count("\n"), "lines")